Subject: [PATCH] firmware: qcom: scm: Use the SIP owner for OCMEM lock

The OCMEM lock and unlock descriptors leave .owner at zero, so the SMC
call is built with ARM_SMCCC_OWNER_ARCH. Google's GPL angler 3.10
driver uses SCM_SIP_FNID() (owner 2) for the same service, and the
availability check already uses ARM_SMCCC_OWNER_SIP, so it reports the
call as available while the actual call returns -EIO.

Set ARM_SMCCC_OWNER_SIP on both descriptors. On msm8994 the Adreno
probe got -5 from qcom_scm_ocmem_lock() and failed with -22.

Evidence: android-msm-angler-3.10-oreo-mr1
drivers/soc/qcom/ocmem_core.c do_lock()/do_unlock(), and
include/soc/qcom/scm.h SCM_SIP_FNID().

diff --git a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
--- a/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
+++ b/drivers/firmware/qcom/qcom_scm.c
@@ -1463,6 +1463,7 @@
 	struct qcom_scm_desc desc = {
 		.svc = QCOM_SCM_SVC_OCMEM,
 		.cmd = QCOM_SCM_OCMEM_LOCK_CMD,
+		.owner = ARM_SMCCC_OWNER_SIP,
 		.args[0] = id,
 		.args[1] = offset,
 		.args[2] = size,
@@ -1487,6 +1488,7 @@
 	struct qcom_scm_desc desc = {
 		.svc = QCOM_SCM_SVC_OCMEM,
 		.cmd = QCOM_SCM_OCMEM_UNLOCK_CMD,
+		.owner = ARM_SMCCC_OWNER_SIP,
 		.args[0] = id,
 		.args[1] = offset,
 		.args[2] = size,
